items: js-long-arith-no-64bit-wrap
paths: file:v1/runtime/backend/js/src/main/resources/scalascript/js-runtime/core-dispatch.mjs file:v1/runtime/backend/js/BUGS.md file:tests/conformance/long-overflow-wrap.ssc file:tests/conformance/expected/long-overflow-wrap.txt file:tests/conformance/contract-roster.tsv file:tests/conformance/corpus-baseline.tsv
scope: |
  `_arith`'s bigint branch returns unmasked BigInt for + - * / %, so ssc Long does not wrap at
  64 bits on the JS lane: it diverges from INT/JVM AND grows without bound. Measured on the
  bench corpus LCG (tuple-monoid): 6,131,220-bit `s` and 43.5 s per pass vs 64 bits and 5 ms
  masked. Fix = BigInt.asIntN(64, …) on the arithmetic ops (`_bit` already does this), gated by
  a new lane-independent conformance case with a golden.
  Widened 2026-07-31: the case is named `long-overflow-wrap` (not `js-…`) because it runs on
  every lane, and adding a case needs the roster + baseline rows.
next: implement + gate, then re-run bench.sh (its js column measured the bug)
